From d33a6ae86b7f96e632628d0644801f3be5f34fb0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kauan Turcato Storto <159664484+KauanDev1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 13:01:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] fix: exact bool indexing, second-constant addressing and
 loop repeat

Under LR_LEGACYRECOMP:

- bool constants: the 8-bit bool address of cond_exec/cond_jmp is an index
  into the 256-bit bool file, the same in both stages (g_Bool(<address>)),
  no per-stage bank;
- ALU constant operands: a constant operand uses const_0_rel_abs only when
  no earlier operand (src1, src2, src3 order) is a constant, otherwise
  const_1_rel_abs (also for the scalar-constant ops);
- loop_start with is_repeat keeps the current aL instead of loading the
  start value (aL is still saved and restored around the loop);
- loops in shaders with jumps restore aL when they fall through;
- each translated container's line reports how many loop ids came from
  definition-table literals ("literal-loops N").

LegacyRecomp patch; same license as XenosRecomp (MIT).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
